//   D. the enemies to expect and the readiness (wing, rank, stance, missiles, ore, shield) with a warning for what is off
//   E. the screens (card space-game-briefing-walkthrough): three screens to walk through (where and why, what to do, how): Enter or Right next, Left back, Enter on the last or L launches, Esc closes; + - 0 and the wheel zoom the map; M goes round its three views; opens at once when a mission is picked on the board (and for a replay), reads one line, never opens in a dock's room
//   The keys box and the lines (cards one-list-keys and list-shortcuts): an order of a list shows the key that opens the list it is IN (Q the fleet's, E the fighters', R the escorts', U the dock's, O the power's: campKeyVia) and is named by its row's own words; no line names a digit as a key.
